# main_loop_chtpm.pal - muchi-pals CHTPM-MODULE VARIANT, modeled
# directly on pal-chain's own pal/main_loop_chtpm.pal (real, live-
# verified precedent for this whole family's href+${piece_methods}
# chtpm standard - see xyzos-standards.txt sec.6/12/16/18/19). ONE
# persistent process, shared identically by EVERY .chtpm layout's own
# <module> tag - screen switching is chtpm's own real href job, never
# this script's (sec.18); this script never restarts across a
# navigation, only chtpm_parser_pal's own liveness-checked
# launch_module() guard keeps it that way (sec.19). Supersedes this
# project's own earlier interact+module/"Control Pets" version (sec.16
# retired that pattern for pure discrete-menu games like this one, in
# favor of ${piece_methods} - see xyzos-standards.txt sec.0-CORRECTED
# item 3 and sec.16 for why <module>/<interact> themselves still stay).
#
#   - read_history reads pieces/apps/player_app/interact_relay.txt via
#     the literal-path 3-arg form (x1 = read cursor, never persisted
#     beyond this run - a fresh module launch always starts at 0). See
#     this project's own system/prisc+x.c top-of-file comment for why a
#     SEPARATE file from history.txt is required here (double-dispatch
#     bug, not a style choice).
#   - muchi_menu_input 0, every loop iteration, cheaply re-derives the
#     current screen from pieces/display/current_layout.txt (a genuine
#     no-op when nothing changed - see that op's own header comment),
#     only bumping pieces/display/muchi_screen_changed.txt on a real
#     screen change.
#   - read_pos's own literal-path argument (fixed this same session -
#     see system/prisc+x.c's own "LOCAL FIX" comment on read_pos's
#     parser; it silently ignored any path before this and always
#     measured history.txt instead) gates muchi_compose_frame/hit_frame
#     so idle ticks (~33/sec) don't re-render when nothing happened.
#   - x3/x4 epoch tick counter: carried over from this project's own
#     original main_loop_chtpm.pal/main_loop.pal (every ~100 loop
#     iterations * ~30ms sleep =~ 3s) - real pet metabolism (hunger/
#     energy/poop, tick_pets.c) must keep advancing regardless of which
#     screen is showing or whether any key was pressed; losing the TICK
#     ITSELF would be a real functionality regression, not just a UI
#     reskin.
#   FLICKER FIX (mass-refactor 2026-07-26, direct user report + direct
#   correction: "there shouldn't be a forced re render. we should render
#   when frame changes and marker file is appended. see 1.tpmos projects
#   if this is unfamiliar 2 u"): do_tick used to `j render` unconditionally
#   after every tick_pets call, forcing a full compose_frame/hit_frame
#   (and therefore a renderer_pulse.txt bump -> a visible scroll-spammed
#   "FRAME UPDATE" redraw) every ~3s even when nothing on the CURRENT
#   screen changed - real 1.TPMOS's own render philosophy (and this
#   file's own sibling, system/chtpm_parser_pal.c's giant "RENDER
#   TRIGGER - MARKER-DRIVEN, SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH" comment: "compose_
#   frame() ONLY fires when frame_changed.txt grows... DO NOT add dirty=1
#   ... caused triple-rendering") is marker-driven only: a render happens
#   because something that's actually visible changed and appended to a
#   marker file, never on a bare timer. do_tick now falls through to
#   after_tick instead of forcing render: the pet state itself keeps
#   decaying silently every ~3s (real, unaffected), but the visible frame
#   only redraws on genuine player input (muchi_menu_input via a keypress
#   or a real screen change), same as every other idle tick already did.
# DOUBLE-RENDER FIX (mass-refactor 2026-07-26, "flicker on nearly every
# keypress" - root cause found via direct pty frame capture on an href
# navigation: two distinct FRAME UPDATE prints for one Enter keypress,
# the FIRST showing "[No Methods]" and the SECOND showing the real
# populated screen). This is a fresh launch every time (this module gets
# killed+relaunched on every href transition - see chtpm_parser_pal.c's
# own cleanup_module() comment), and the unconditional muchi_compose_frame
# below USED TO run before this module's own first muchi_menu_input(0)
# idle-sync call - meaning the very first compose read piece.pdl/state
# content from BEFORE this screen's own dynamic METHOD rows had ever been
# generated for it (regenerate_pets_piece_pdl/write_chtpm_bridge, both
# inside muchi_menu_input.c, only run once muchi_menu_input actually
# executes). Running the idle-sync ONCE before the first compose - not
# just every loop iteration afterward - means the FIRST render is already
# correct, with no stale/incomplete flash beforehand.
li x1, 0
li x3, 0
li x4, 100

li x9, 0
muchi_menu_input x9
muchi_compose_frame
hit_frame
read_pos x7, "pieces/display/muchi_screen_changed.txt"

loop:
li x9, 0
muchi_menu_input x9
read_pos x8, "pieces/display/muchi_screen_changed.txt"
beq x7, x8, check_key
addi x7, x8, 0
j render

check_key:
read_history pieces/apps/player_app/interact_relay.txt x2, x1
beq x2, x0, no_key
muchi_menu_input x2
j render

no_key:
addi x3, x3, 1
beq x3, x4, do_tick
j after_tick

do_tick:
tick_pets
li x3, 0
j after_tick

after_tick:
sleep 30000
j loop

render:
muchi_compose_frame
hit_frame
sleep 30000
j loop
